            <ArticleTitle>Extensive infiltration of bone with marrow necrosis in a case of hairy cell leukaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>228-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This 32-year-old patient with hairy cell leukaemia demonstrated extensive bony involvement in a pattern not previously described. Although the disease continued to progress during interferon treatment, a change to a regime of deoxycoformycin resulted in an excellent response.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
